---
import CopyableCommand from "../../components/CopyableCommand.astro";
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Docs — clawforge" description="Get started with clawforge.">
  <article class="py-8">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold">Getting started</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
      Install Claude Code assets — skills, agents, hooks, MCP servers — with one command.
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">1. Install the CLI</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
        The CLI ships as <code class="rounded bg-zinc-100 px-1 dark:bg-zinc-800">@clawforge/cli</code>.
        Use <code class="rounded bg-zinc-100 px-1 dark:bg-zinc-800">npx</code> for one-off
        installs or install globally.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3">
        <CopyableCommand command="npm install -g @clawforge/cli" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">2. Initialise your manifest</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
        A manifest records everything clawforge installs for you. This is what makes installs
        reversible.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3">
        <CopyableCommand command="clawforge init" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">3. Find entries</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Search the registry from the CLI, or browse online.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3">
        <CopyableCommand command="clawforge search tdd" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">4. Install one</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Install an entry by id. Use <code class="rounded bg-zinc-100 px-1 dark:bg-zinc-800">--track</code>
        so the manifest can remove it cleanly later.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3">
        <CopyableCommand command="clawforge add skill:tdd-workflow --track" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">5. Remove when done</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
        Clean removal: files deleted, JSON merges reverted to their <code
          class="rounded bg-zinc-100 px-1 dark:bg-zinc-800">before</code
        > snapshot.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-3">
        <CopyableCommand command="clawforge remove skill:tdd-workflow" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-zinc-200 p-6 dark:border-zinc-800">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Supported entry kinds</h3>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li>
          <code class="font-mono">skill:</code> — SKILL.md files under <code class="font-mono"
            >~/.claude/skills/</code
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <code class="font-mono">agent:</code> — subagent definitions under <code
            class="font-mono">~/.claude/agents/</code
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <code class="font-mono">cmd:</code> — slash commands under <code class="font-mono"
            >./.claude/commands/</code
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <code class="font-mono">hook:</code> — PreToolUse / PostToolUse snippets merged into
          <code class="font-mono">settings.json</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <code class="font-mono">mcp:</code> — MCP server configs merged into <code
            class="font-mono">settings.json</code
          >
        </li>
        <li>
          <code class="font-mono">preset:</code> — bundles of the above
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>
